# .trivyignore — suppress known false positives or accepted risks.
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line. Add a comment explaining why it is accepted.
# Keep this list as short as possible — prefer fixing over ignoring.
#
# Example:
# CVE-2023-XXXX  # unfixed in Alpine 3.18; no patch upstream yet, low exploitability

# ── Terraform IaC suppressions ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The S3 frontend bucket intentionally uses public-read ACL for static website
# hosting. Trivy flags this as a misconfiguration but it is by design.
AVD-AWS-0094    # S3 bucket has public access block disabled (frontend website bucket)
AVD-AWS-0132    # S3 bucket is not encrypted (public static assets — no sensitive data)

# RDS deletion protection is off in dev/staging by design (cost/ease of teardown).
# Production has deletion_protection = true in terraform/environments/prod/main.tf.
# AVD-AWS-0177  # uncomment to suppress RDS deletion-protection check across all envs
